WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.068
- You are a, oh, look at this!

00:00:03.068 --> 00:00:06.033
What is this, what is this?

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:09.803
How are they?

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.456
They're not bad!

00:00:14.456 --> 00:00:17.039
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.450
Hi, I'm Neil Patrick
Harris, and I've been asked

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:28.700
to read questions while
playing with puppies.

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:31.470
And how do you say no to that?

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.106
Hi!

00:00:34.106 --> 00:00:35.726
You're so cute!

00:00:35.726 --> 00:00:36.559
Oh!

00:00:41.063 --> 00:00:44.280
Here's a question, what's
one of your weirdest

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.440
or funniest fan encounters?

00:00:47.440 --> 00:00:50.933
I had an old timey fan
once, he was squeaky.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:54.910
So then I got one of the newer
Dyson fans, that's better.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:01:00.120
If you had to give Count
Olaf one genuine compliment,

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:01.033
what would it be?

00:01:02.150 --> 00:01:05.050
He is devilishly handsome.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:08.500
He has metal, you know what that means?

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.903
Not metal like your collar,
but metal, gumption.

00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:15.260
What are you plans after the third season,

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:16.600
I'm assuming last season it will catch up

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:18.240
to the last books of A
Series of Unfortunate Events?

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:21.073
And when it wraps filming,
will you go back to Broadway?

00:01:22.510 --> 00:01:26.490
Um, that's my lace, of my shoe, thank you.

00:01:26.490 --> 00:01:29.033
Um, I'd love to go back
to Broadway some day.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.481
I'm looking forward to resting.

00:01:32.481 --> 00:01:34.540
A Series of Unfortunate
Events is super fun,

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:37.389
but all kinds of exhausting,

00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:42.389
much like, you know when you
really have to take a dump?

00:01:42.917 --> 00:01:47.110
But you can't, because you're not outside?

00:01:47.110 --> 00:01:51.170
You know that feeling,
and you really gotta go?

00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:52.160
And then you finally go and you're like,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:55.837
oh I need a rest, that's
kinda my life right now.

00:01:56.930 --> 00:02:01.150
Hey question, what's the craziest rumor

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:03.183
you've heard about yourself?

00:02:04.410 --> 00:02:08.573
Um, that i was on Malcolm in the Middle.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:13.850
In a movie about your life, who

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:16.373
would you want to play and David?

00:02:17.470 --> 00:02:20.770
Oh, that's a good question,
who would play me?

00:02:20.770 --> 00:02:24.653
Josh Dummel, and who would play David?

00:02:25.550 --> 00:02:27.432
Nick Jonas, next question!

00:02:27.432 --> 00:02:28.753
(laughs)

00:02:28.753 --> 00:02:31.170
(soft music)

00:02:34.447 --> 00:02:36.018
C'mon, c'mon.

00:02:36.018 --> 00:02:38.840
This is my favorite, are we
allowed to pick a favorite?

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.560
Because this one, fine,
okay it's the other one.

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.970
Fine, it's the other one then.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:46.340
What in your opinion, was
Count Olaf's best disguise?

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:47.640
They were all pretty good.

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:53.407
I think I like the Detective
DuPaul the best, right?

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:56.223
He's in the bile village episodes.

00:02:57.300 --> 00:02:59.990
And he's a hipster man
and he talks like this!

00:02:59.990 --> 00:03:03.833
Everything he says boop
da da boop boop, cool.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:07.340
Is there a celebrity that you've met

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.963
that left you completely starstruck?

00:03:10.820 --> 00:03:11.673
David Franco.

00:03:14.544 --> 00:03:17.080
Easy to look at.

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:19.963
To put it bluntly, Count
Olaf is a garbage human.

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.070
How do you get into character to

00:03:22.070 --> 00:03:23.713
play such a despicable person?

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:27.000
It's kinda easy because
if your ever grumpy,

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:32.000
or wishing, or if you're
down and negative,

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:35.440
you can just channel
that into the character.

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:36.500
How often do you get to play someone

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.273
who is downright awful, answer me!

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:43.020
Do you still talk to the HIMYM cast?

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:44.510
Would you ever consider collaborating

00:03:44.510 --> 00:03:47.230
or reuniting with the cast down the line?

00:03:47.230 --> 00:03:50.690
I do still talk to the HIMYM
cast, mostly Cobie Smulders,

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:54.927
because when you have kids
that are similar ages,

00:03:54.927 --> 00:03:59.223
and she and Taran her husband
lived in New York for a bit,

00:04:01.380 --> 00:04:03.653
but yeah we text and shoot the breeze.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:07.697
I don't think we'd ever
reunite on the show.

00:04:07.697 --> 00:04:11.700
Now you are, you are a
troublemaker, yes you are.

00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:12.663
Yes, thank you.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.720
These are so cute these dogs.

00:04:15.720 --> 00:04:17.970
You played a lot of really
different characters,

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:19.610
do you have a favorite one?

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:23.803
My favorite is probably,
Shirley St. Ives was fun.

00:04:24.970 --> 00:04:29.540
She was a girl, and I sorta
got to play a mad man.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:33.675
She talked like this, it was
less fun when I had to pee.

00:04:33.675 --> 00:04:36.483
Because I was wearing padding and spanx.

00:04:38.821 --> 00:04:41.493
And kind of tucking, you know.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.410
Do you appreciate it when fans

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:51.610
come up to you in public,
or is it annoying?

00:04:51.610 --> 00:04:53.210
No it's never annoying I like fans

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.230
when they come up, I like
when people say nice things.

00:04:55.230 --> 00:04:57.940
Less fun is when they just
try to take your picture

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.200
while you're eating at a restaurant,

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.280
because that's never a good picture.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:03.860
I'm like talking, in the
middle of a conversation,

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.807
scowling, I look over, and someones like.

00:05:09.178 --> 00:05:10.283
But if someone comes up
and says something nice,

00:05:11.744 --> 00:05:13.063
that's always fun to hear, right?

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.790
Uh this one, this one, lover boy, girl?

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:23.300
Would you ever host the Tony's again?

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.950
Oh I would love to do that again.

00:05:25.944 --> 00:05:26.993
It's a hard job though.

00:05:28.075 --> 00:05:30.325
Maybe some day, I need
to take some time off.

00:05:31.160 --> 00:05:34.300
The Tony's are great fun,
great show for the host.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.610
Because there's all the performances,

00:05:35.610 --> 00:05:37.610
it is the best show to watch because

00:05:37.610 --> 00:05:40.780
it's all performances by people
who are doing shows live.

00:05:40.780 --> 00:05:45.647
So then you get the live
show, all around you.

00:05:46.790 --> 00:05:49.380
What did you learn as a young actor

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:50.740
in Doogie Howser, M.D. that
helped you later in life

00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:52.680
as an adult actor?

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:54.253
How to suture my own wounds.

00:05:58.390 --> 00:06:01.883
How to neuter dogs, that
hasn't helped me that much.

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:07.000
What has been the most
memorable moment in your life

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:08.990
that you would like to cherish forever?

00:06:08.990 --> 00:06:11.133
Oh man, the birth of my children.

00:06:12.368 --> 00:06:17.368
Holding newborn babies,
that came from you,

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:19.860
that's a pretty amazing thing.

00:06:19.860 --> 00:06:22.000
Kids by the way would love you guys.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.220
Thank God they're not here,
because I would be leaving

00:06:24.220 --> 00:06:26.270
with four more dogs.

00:06:26.270 --> 00:06:28.430
How do you go about choosing the themes

00:06:28.430 --> 00:06:30.810
for your family's Halloween
costumes each year?

00:06:30.810 --> 00:06:34.270
And can you hint at some
potential options for this year?

00:06:34.270 --> 00:06:38.170
No hints, we have talked about it.

00:06:38.170 --> 00:06:40.373
It's much more of a
negotiation now because,

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:45.370
the kids speak the English
language and have opinions.

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:47.930
Before it was so much easier, here,

00:06:47.930 --> 00:06:52.700
put on this Hawaiian costume,
here you look like Dorothy.

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:57.483
Snap, now it's, c'mon, it'll be fun.

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:02.290
You're gonna do this, you're
gonna wear this, put this on.

00:07:02.290 --> 00:07:04.084
No we don't do that.

00:07:04.084 --> 00:07:06.460
What do you think happened with
Barney after the show ended,

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:09.120
and what would he be up to now?

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:13.230
Um, probably same old same
old, what would he be up to?

00:07:13.230 --> 00:07:17.313
Two fingers of scotch, and probably,

00:07:18.900 --> 00:07:19.743
fifteen chicks.

00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:22.610
What's your go-to karaoke song?

00:07:23.650 --> 00:07:26.300
That's a good question,
Rocket Man is good.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:29.533
I tend to go with Elton John
songs, because they're fun.

00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:33.423
I also know all the words to
The Devil went down to Georgia.

00:07:35.495 --> 00:07:39.253
That was my New Mexico rap days.

00:07:41.025 --> 00:07:42.280
He was in a bind, because
he was way behind.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:43.480
He was willing to make a deal,

00:07:43.480 --> 00:07:45.020
when he came across the Joe Man's song,

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:46.240
we're still gonna play it hot!

00:07:46.240 --> 00:07:47.940
What's your idea of a perfect day?

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:50.290
Playing with puppies.

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:54.490
Or probably a perfect day would be,

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:59.490
with my family, in Hawaii,
on the beach, drinking a

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:06.690
pina colada, and writing
Disney theme park attractions.

00:08:09.020 --> 00:08:11.000
I don't think there's a
Disney theme park in Hawaii,

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:13.080
but that would be a perfect day.

00:08:13.080 --> 00:08:15.670
Okay, that's my arm, thank you.

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:18.090
Out of all the villains in
Count Olaf's theater troupe,

00:08:18.090 --> 00:08:19.880
who is your favorite?

00:08:19.880 --> 00:08:22.888
I got a soft spot for Hook Hand Man,

00:08:22.888 --> 00:08:26.460
because he is my right hook man.

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:29.470
Last question, if you were willingly going

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:31.050
to visit a deserted island for a few days

00:08:31.050 --> 00:08:32.640
and could only have three things with you,

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:34.520
what would you bring?

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.710
Three things on a deserted island.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:41.710
A lighter, or a tarp, one of those phones,

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.920
that you can call people that saves you.

00:08:44.920 --> 00:08:48.813
Luxury items I'd probably
bring, I don't know, a ukulele?

00:08:50.130 --> 00:08:53.663
No, he said no I'm biting his shoe.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:57.443
Um, maybe a flashlight.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:03.870
Alright, those are all
my questions, thank you

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:06.090
for asking them, and thanks
for all these puppies

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:11.090
who are all available if you
want to own one of these,

00:09:11.310 --> 00:09:13.130
they're all from the
North Shore Animal League.

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:14.910
So thanks to the amazing people there

00:09:14.910 --> 00:09:17.140
for doing that, and come give yourself an

00:09:17.140 --> 00:09:20.171
angry, biting dog, ow!

00:09:20.171 --> 00:09:22.108
(laughs)

00:09:22.108 --> 00:09:22.941
See ya.

00:09:23.981 --> 00:09:26.398
(soft music)

